{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","symbolKind":"protocol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L53","fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift"}},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertices","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedPseudograph"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, with no hashing, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_key(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_vertex(atKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its inverse.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the members of the same name without the label, for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex’s key is now "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"; otherwise it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, trapping on any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":", then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each vertex in order, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each pair"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in order: the same graph, and the same position for each pair."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key density.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", plus O(1) per live vertex: the memory of the representation’s own page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span can exceed the vertex count: removals leave holes, and a decoded graph may start at any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position (its decoder bounds the span at ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × vertexCount + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages). Keys before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest live key cost nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key rows."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typed as "},{"code":"SuccessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"PredecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes; "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not requirements."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(edge:)"},{"text":" differs in its return type: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple, returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new position, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. So generic code inserts an edge by key, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hooks are underscored because they are for wrappers inside the library: callers use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representations’ own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"type":"text","text":" members, which take vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"remove(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and every edge at it."}],"role":"symbol","required":true,"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(_:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"go forward.","type":"text"}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAll(keepin